title: TUI + mods references in; voice on sherpa-onnx with a Mac boost
summary: 'The TUI and mods scout landed (research 21). It recommends lifting pi-tui as the renderer, pi-agent-core and pi-ai for the local loop, OpenCode''s client/server topology, and out-of-process mods with a closed view kit. Founder chose a sherpa-onnx voice core with FluidAudio as an optional Mac backend, so voice works on Windows. Open flag: whether shipping subscription-driven headless Claude sessions to the world in 8.1 fits Anthropic''s terms needs checking before 8.1.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D31
    decision: Voice client is built on sherpa-onnx (Silero VAD, Parakeet STT, diarization, Kokoro TTS via ONNX, Node bindings) on Mac/Windows/Linux, with FluidAudio on the Neural Engine as an optional Mac backend behind the same interface; capabilities verified in the Move 1 probe
    rationale: P8-R4 Windows requirement; one engine, platform boost optional.
learnings:
  - deepseek-harness dropped its pi-tui TUI after long sessions rendered slowly (12 s for 196k events, 800 ms/keystroke until width-keyed line caches); Gnomon's TUI needs virtualization and line caching from day one.
  - None of the reference harnesses sandbox mods; running Gnomon mods out of process over stdio JSON-RPC with declared, enforced effects would be a genuine first.
  - Headless Claude Code loses live streaming unless --include-partial-messages is passed; the spec's runner argv must add it for the TUI.
  - 'Open question for 8.1: confirm that distributing a harness that drives users'' subscription Claude Code headless fits Anthropic''s terms.'
